WEBVTT

00:00:01.464 --> 00:00:05.078
It seems today
 that all you see

00:00:05.154 --> 00:00:08.155
Is violence in movies
 and sex on TV

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:11.901
But where are those
 good old-fashioned values

00:00:11.903 --> 00:00:14.829
On which we used to rely?

00:00:14.906 --> 00:00:18.258
Lucky there's a family guy

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:21.836
Lucky there's a man who
 positively can do

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.055
All the things that make us

00:00:23.239 --> 00:00:24.749
Laugh and cry

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:30.747
He's... a...
 Fam... ily... Guy.

00:00:39.514 --> 00:00:42.515
It was nice of the brewery
to host this Oktoberfest.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.890
Yeah, they wanted to support
the community

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:45.944
and hopefully win back
some of the market share

00:00:45.946 --> 00:00:48.838
-they lost to fentanyl.
-Those come in rainbow now.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.524
Yeah, I reposted an article
about that on Facebook

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:55.079
and said "FYI," so I basically
saved the children.

00:00:55.413 --> 00:00:57.013
This festival's kind of weird.

00:00:57.225 --> 00:00:59.558
How did Germans even come up
with Oktoberfest?

00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:00.424
So, guys,

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:01.801
turns out everybody hates us

00:01:01.878 --> 00:01:03.787
for all our world wars,
et cetera.

00:01:03.789 --> 00:01:05.305
We need to do something
that shows

00:01:05.381 --> 00:01:08.303
we are fun and silly,
and not human exterminators.

00:01:08.328 --> 00:01:09.793
What about beer, pretzels,

00:01:09.818 --> 00:01:12.177
und horns that go
"oompa oompa"?

00:01:12.202 --> 00:01:13.535
That's good. Very good.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.364
Yes, that, and little square
mustaches because--

00:01:17.389 --> 00:01:18.726
No more mustaches!

00:01:19.117 --> 00:01:20.300
Meg, check it out.

00:01:20.396 --> 00:01:22.914
A make-your-own sausage station.

00:01:22.971 --> 00:01:24.637
Are you supposed to be
touching that?

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.143
Ha, they look like
little poops--

00:01:29.599 --> 00:01:31.832
You must make me whole again.

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:36.912
Never mind, this is my destiny!

00:01:40.102 --> 00:01:41.433
Hey, look, a chiropractor.

00:01:41.509 --> 00:01:42.826
I could actually use
an adjustment.

00:01:43.032 --> 00:01:45.103
Huh, let's see how you turn this
into a brag.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:48.158
I hurt my back reading
screenplays for a competition.

00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:49.590
Finish the sentence.

00:01:49.668 --> 00:01:51.906
-That I paid to be a judge in.
-There you go.

00:01:52.766 --> 00:01:54.072
-Hello.
-Cha-ching!

00:01:54.097 --> 00:01:56.764
I mean, hello. Would you guys
like an adjustment?

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.950
-I'll take one.
-Not me. I think you're a quack.

00:01:59.027 --> 00:02:01.361
I also do colonic
irrigation therapy.

00:02:01.437 --> 00:02:02.746
I'll take a pamphlet.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.124
This head hole smells like spit.

00:02:06.386 --> 00:02:10.019
Don't worry, I always give it
one lazy wipe between patients.

00:02:10.021 --> 00:02:11.630
Now, I'm gonna ask you
some questions

00:02:11.706 --> 00:02:13.873
I can steer
into any direction I need.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.042
-Do you ever feel tired?
-I do.

00:02:16.119 --> 00:02:18.027
And if you go a few hours
between meals,

00:02:18.029 --> 00:02:20.363
do you ever feel
like you need to eat again?

00:02:20.365 --> 00:02:21.531
Yeah, like, every day.

00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:23.366
That's a big problem nowadays.

00:02:23.626 --> 00:02:26.019
I have some very expensive
supplements that'll help.

00:02:28.056 --> 00:02:29.555
Whoa. That feels great.

00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:31.632
Yeah, that good feeling
will last

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.467
right until you get
into your car.

00:02:33.545 --> 00:02:35.970
-Here's your bill.
-$700?

00:02:36.047 --> 00:02:39.157
That covers the consultation,
evaluation, diagnosis,

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.885
adjustment, supplements
and a fart surcharge.

00:02:41.887 --> 00:02:43.477
-I didn't fart.
-You did.

00:02:43.555 --> 00:02:45.722
People always do.
Or maybe I did.

00:02:45.724 --> 00:02:47.815
Either way, I'll just bill it
to your insurance.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.110
Man, I can't believe--

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.985
- Oh, there it is.
- Told you.

00:02:51.062 --> 00:02:52.912
Did you see how much
that chiropractor charged?

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:54.475
I could do
the same thing he did.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.399
You could, and that's not
a compliment.

00:02:56.418 --> 00:02:58.659
His degree was
from a Margaritaville.

00:02:59.452 --> 00:03:01.495
Should... should we become
chiropractors?

00:03:01.573 --> 00:03:04.424
Already on it. "Siri,
how do I become a chiropractor?"

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.742
Do you want to be a doctor,

00:03:05.744 --> 00:03:07.501
but don't like to read books?

00:03:07.526 --> 00:03:09.209
-Yes.
 -Congratulations.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:10.787
You are now a chiropractor.

00:03:10.904 --> 00:03:13.525
Mailing certification
 and teeth whitening kit now.

00:03:13.743 --> 00:03:14.893
Oh, that was easy.

00:03:14.918 --> 00:03:15.960
Yeah, thank God.

00:03:16.037 --> 00:03:17.962
I needed a new job,
and it was either this

00:03:18.039 --> 00:03:19.705
or become a family photographer.

00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:21.966
Is your son just the cutest,

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.005
and are you eager to capture
 that precious sliver of time?

00:03:25.083 --> 00:03:27.507
Well, at Son in Front
 of a Tree Photography,

00:03:27.532 --> 00:03:29.032
we capture
 these memories for you

00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:31.200
by photographing your son
 in front of a tree

00:03:31.202 --> 00:03:32.960
in a park that's close
 to my house.

00:03:33.038 --> 00:03:34.704
Put him in a shirt that he hates

00:03:34.706 --> 00:03:37.315
and watch him lean, climb,
 or sit in front of a tree.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:40.504
Hold his arms as he jumps
into the air in front of a tree.

00:03:40.789 --> 00:03:43.488
Sure, he bit you for making him
take off his Spider-Man shoes,

00:03:44.048 --> 00:03:44.730
but wait until you see

00:03:44.807 --> 00:03:46.883
this photo of him
 resting on his hands

00:03:46.885 --> 00:03:48.067
in front of a tree.

00:03:48.144 --> 00:03:49.235
We'll even take one

00:03:49.312 --> 00:03:50.812
of the parents
 in front of the tree.

00:03:50.837 --> 00:03:53.033
Because at Son in Front
 of a Tree Photography,

00:03:53.058 --> 00:03:55.683
we capture memories
 that'll last a lifetime.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.984
And years later,

00:03:57.062 --> 00:03:58.986
when that same son is
 forced out of college

00:03:59.064 --> 00:04:00.563
for a team hazing scandal,

00:04:00.565 --> 00:04:03.508
you'll look at the photos
 of your son in front of a tre

00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:06.275
and wonder if that monster ws
 always inside him.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.483
Yeah, probably.

00:04:07.604 --> 00:04:09.271
He bit you
 for taking off his shoes.

00:04:09.407 --> 00:04:10.213
Call today.

00:04:10.238 --> 00:04:11.463
May not ever receive photos.

00:04:12.927 --> 00:04:14.853
Ha-ha! Oh.

00:04:14.929 --> 00:04:17.580
God, the prizes at these things
are such junk.

00:04:17.582 --> 00:04:20.007
I want one. Peter, win me a toy.

00:04:20.085 --> 00:04:21.008
What? Why?

00:04:21.304 --> 00:04:23.547
'Cause I'm
New England-lady drunk.

00:04:23.572 --> 00:04:25.771
Either you win me a stupid,
stuffed something,

00:04:25.825 --> 00:04:28.234
or I'm gonna start naming
ex-boyfriends who would've.

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:29.683
Great, everybody,
get ready to hear

00:04:29.761 --> 00:04:31.944
who made First Team All-Dirtbag.

00:04:32.021 --> 00:04:34.113
Tom Hambley would've
had me double-fisting

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.857
highly flammable
bootleg SpongeBobs by now.

00:04:36.935 --> 00:04:39.613
Yeah, didn't he also whip it out
to your mom before your prom?

00:04:39.638 --> 00:04:41.713
He said he mistimed
how far away he was

00:04:41.738 --> 00:04:44.147
from our hallway bathroom.
Just throw the ball.

00:04:44.275 --> 00:04:45.942
I would,
but my elbow's acting up.

00:04:45.944 --> 00:04:47.793
Old injury from
The Late Night Wars.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.703
I'll win you one
of them things, Lois.

00:04:49.781 --> 00:04:51.797
Oh, no, it's Mikey Bagshaw,

00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:55.209
Lois's ex-boyfriend with
shamrock tattoos on both calves.

00:04:55.286 --> 00:04:56.381
You're allowed here?

00:04:56.406 --> 00:04:57.739
Yeah, there ain't
no schools close.

00:04:58.073 --> 00:05:00.073
Then I guess
it's your move, Peter.

00:05:00.581 --> 00:05:02.046
This is really testing me.

00:05:02.218 --> 00:05:05.096
I wonder what my old karate
sensei would want me to do.

00:05:05.155 --> 00:05:08.347
Take your sneakers off, Peter.
You can't wear them on the mats.

00:05:08.379 --> 00:05:09.879
But they light up, sensei.

00:05:09.904 --> 00:05:13.879
Put them in the cubbies. Geez,
every class with this clown.

00:05:22.981 --> 00:05:25.406
He throws like a girl!

00:05:25.483 --> 00:05:27.333
Come on, people don't say that
anymore, dude.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:30.345
The correct term is he throws
like a Chalamet, probably.

00:05:37.091 --> 00:05:39.136
And on behalf of everyone
 at Channel Five,

00:05:39.214 --> 00:05:41.322
we'd like to apologize
 for the pornography

00:05:41.399 --> 00:05:43.140
that aired during
 our cooking segment.

00:05:43.218 --> 00:05:44.734
There are a lot
 of very funny people

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.954
who are good at computers,
 and we can't stop them.

00:05:47.196 --> 00:05:49.055
All right, who's ready
for The Last of Us?

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.907
I love zombie shows
about shrub overgrowth.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:53.726
Chris, move,
you're sitting in my spot.

00:05:53.728 --> 00:05:55.486
Yeah, I think
I'm gonna be sitting

00:05:55.563 --> 00:05:57.897
wherever I want
from now on, chief.

00:05:57.899 --> 00:05:59.507
What? Where am I
supposed to sit?

00:05:59.584 --> 00:06:01.509
Kind of not my problem, chief.

00:06:01.586 --> 00:06:03.085
Did you just double "chief" me?

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.974
-That's right, chief.
-Triple?

00:06:04.999 --> 00:06:06.173
Is this 'cause of the throw?

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:08.382
Well, technically,
it didn't qualify as a throw.

00:06:08.459 --> 00:06:11.868
It fell somewhere between a roll
and a...

00:06:11.926 --> 00:06:13.456
Come on,
barely anybody saw that.

00:06:13.481 --> 00:06:14.905
I'm sure it'll all blow over.

00:06:15.207 --> 00:06:17.498
And now in "Ha-Ha,
 Look At This Guy" news,

00:06:17.523 --> 00:06:18.968
ha-ha, look at this guy.

00:06:22.069 --> 00:06:23.218
Aw, rats.

00:06:23.243 --> 00:06:25.307
If that isn't an indication
 of how poorly

00:06:25.332 --> 00:06:27.832
someone's penis works,
 I don't know what is.

00:06:27.962 --> 00:06:29.478
Is this my fault, Peter?

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.775
Is it 'cause I made you
watch Ted Lasso?

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.074
You know, maybe sports shows

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:35.026
should be about sports
instead of feelings.

00:06:35.102 --> 00:06:37.695
-Look, it's not that big a deal.
-It is, though.

00:06:37.772 --> 00:06:39.513
I always knew
you were overweight,

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.924
but I thought you were
at least athletic fat.

00:06:41.926 --> 00:06:45.185
I told people you were
a good fat, like an avocado.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.818
Now, I don't know what you are.

00:06:47.022 --> 00:06:49.189
Okay, I see that
I don't have the support

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:51.876
of my family on this,
but at least I have my friends.

00:06:51.953 --> 00:06:53.410
I'm gonna see if they
want to meet at The Clam.

00:06:55.421 --> 00:06:56.288
They said they're busy.

00:06:56.584 --> 00:06:58.865
I see GIFs of people
without genitals.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.033
That means busy.

00:07:00.111 --> 00:07:02.714
Does this mean
you're a beta dad now?

00:07:02.792 --> 00:07:05.556
No, Chris. But I want you
to know that I heard you.

00:07:05.633 --> 00:07:08.968
Your feelings are valid,
and thank you-- Oh, God, I am.

00:07:09.044 --> 00:07:10.469
Aw, now I'm gonna
have to hang out

00:07:10.546 --> 00:07:11.958
at the beta dad headquarters:

00:07:12.144 --> 00:07:13.418
the farmers market.

00:07:13.713 --> 00:07:15.104
This isn't spicy, is it?

00:07:15.142 --> 00:07:17.217
No, sir, it's a strawberry.

00:07:17.295 --> 00:07:19.779
Hmm, I better not.
I can't do spicy.

00:07:23.101 --> 00:07:25.076
I can't believe you guys
got this business

00:07:25.152 --> 00:07:26.577
started so quickly.

00:07:26.729 --> 00:07:29.321
Yeah, we found the perfect spot
with zero available parking,

00:07:29.398 --> 00:07:30.915
and the rest
just fell into place.

00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:32.975
Chris, do you know
what the most important part

00:07:32.977 --> 00:07:34.919
of working
in a busy doctor's office is?

00:07:34.996 --> 00:07:36.587
-The patients?
-Nope.

00:07:36.739 --> 00:07:38.330
Taking care of the tropical fish

00:07:38.407 --> 00:07:40.240
that's impossible
to take care of.

00:07:40.265 --> 00:07:42.189
Why is it swimming upside down?

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.837
I don't know. Sometimes
it sinks, sometimes it floats,

00:07:44.913 --> 00:07:46.655
and sometimes it does that.
All are bad.

00:07:46.657 --> 00:07:47.932
There's a number
taped to the desk.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.775
That's Eric,
our tropical fish guy.

00:07:49.777 --> 00:07:50.867
He's gonna be your best friend.

00:07:50.945 --> 00:07:52.611
Call him whenever
it does anything.

00:07:52.613 --> 00:07:53.888
Do everything Eric says.

00:07:53.965 --> 00:07:55.890
None of it will work,
but trust me, he's the best.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:57.613
It flipped back over.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.727
Why are you telling me?
Tell Eric.

00:08:02.959 --> 00:08:05.066
Remember, Peter,
it's not drinking alone

00:08:05.142 --> 00:08:07.158
as long as you have
Popsicle Peter with you.

00:08:07.383 --> 00:08:07.807
Help.

00:08:07.832 --> 00:08:10.738
He only uses me
to scratch his icky parts.

00:08:10.815 --> 00:08:12.406
Shut up
and get to work in there.

00:08:13.057 --> 00:08:14.800
Uh-oh, look who's here.

00:08:14.802 --> 00:08:16.744
What the hell?
You guys said you had plans,

00:08:16.821 --> 00:08:17.970
but you're here drinking?

00:08:17.972 --> 00:08:19.472
And you're in my spot,
Cleveland.

00:08:19.474 --> 00:08:21.082
Yep. Think I'm gonna be sitting

00:08:21.158 --> 00:08:22.992
wherever I want
from now on, chief.

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:24.660
Sorry, we didn't want
people thinking

00:08:24.687 --> 00:08:26.687
we were noodle-armed
by association.

00:08:26.712 --> 00:08:29.213
Yeah, my arms
are literally all I have.

00:08:29.481 --> 00:08:31.423
How do you not know
how to throw?

00:08:31.658 --> 00:08:32.435
I never learned.

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:34.899
My dad was always working
when I was a kid,

00:08:34.924 --> 00:08:36.697
and when he'd get home, he
always said he had a headache.

00:08:37.793 --> 00:08:40.051
That was back before everyone
 carried metal water bottles,

00:08:40.127 --> 00:08:42.778
so no one drank water,
 and all adults had headaches.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.922
My only friends
 were day raccoons,

00:08:45.073 --> 00:08:46.999
who are the most social
 of all raccoons.

00:08:47.075 --> 00:08:49.001
They're the ones
 who taught me how to throw.

00:08:49.077 --> 00:08:50.819
So, that's why
 I throw bad for a guy,

00:08:50.821 --> 00:08:52.596
but really good for a raccoon.

00:08:55.493 --> 00:08:56.992
-Is all that true?
-I don't know.

00:08:56.994 --> 00:08:58.510
I've had
several cases of rabies,

00:08:58.587 --> 00:08:59.920
so memories are hard for me.

00:08:59.997 --> 00:09:01.922
All I know is that I've spent
the rest of my life

00:09:01.999 --> 00:09:03.924
avoiding scenarios
where I got to throw.

00:09:04.001 --> 00:09:06.110
Didn't you go
to Red Sox fantasy camp?

00:09:06.187 --> 00:09:08.003
And I swear I've seen you
having a catch

00:09:08.005 --> 00:09:09.505
with Chris
out on your front lawn.

00:09:09.507 --> 00:09:10.856
Yeah, that was my stunt double.

00:09:10.913 --> 00:09:13.358
He's the fat guy who dresses up
like me at Comic-Con.

00:09:13.403 --> 00:09:15.268
He wants to interview me as me,

00:09:15.293 --> 00:09:16.734
and I'm just like, dude, no.

00:09:16.864 --> 00:09:18.952
Excuse me,
are you Peter Griffin?

00:09:18.977 --> 00:09:21.049
That depends.
Are you classlessly serving

00:09:21.051 --> 00:09:23.185
a legal document
for Jason Sudeikis?

00:09:23.187 --> 00:09:25.796
No, I do promotions
for a local minor league team,

00:09:25.873 --> 00:09:27.277
the Quahog Blowholes.

00:09:27.395 --> 00:09:28.707
Ah, yes, then I'm Peter.

00:09:28.784 --> 00:09:30.359
I wanted to invite you
to throw out

00:09:30.361 --> 00:09:32.861
a ceremonial first pitch
this weekend.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.713
What? You know
he can't throw, right?

00:09:34.789 --> 00:09:36.266
Yes, that's why we want him.

00:09:36.291 --> 00:09:38.867
Minor league baseball
needs gimmicks to attract fans.

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:41.828
You guys remember the story
about that chimpanzee umpire?

00:09:41.964 --> 00:09:43.463
The one what ate up
all them fans' faces?

00:09:43.709 --> 00:09:44.997
Yup. That was me.

00:09:45.242 --> 00:09:48.270
Anyway, we think you'd make
the perfect gimmick, Peter.

00:09:48.295 --> 00:09:49.234
I'll do it.

00:09:49.304 --> 00:09:51.655
What? You're gonna
embarrass yourself again.

00:09:51.732 --> 00:09:53.306
This time on a bigger stage.

00:09:53.384 --> 00:09:55.384
So? Did Batgirl just give up

00:09:55.386 --> 00:09:56.902
when everyone said
her movie stunk?

00:09:56.979 --> 00:09:59.175
Uh, yes. Very publicly, yes.

00:09:59.815 --> 00:10:00.906
Well, I'm not Batgirl.

00:10:00.983 --> 00:10:02.482
I am gonna throw out
that first pitch,

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:04.350
and it's gonna be
a perfect strike.

00:10:04.375 --> 00:10:07.004
I love confident idiots.
It's why I bought a Tesla.

00:10:07.081 --> 00:10:08.154
See you this weekend.

00:10:08.533 --> 00:10:09.680
What are you doing?

00:10:09.705 --> 00:10:12.176
You can't just learn
how to throw in a couple days.

00:10:12.353 --> 00:10:13.777
Hey, anything is possible.

00:10:13.854 --> 00:10:15.946
